module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_host_property_refusal_missing_from_the_infra_allowlist

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode, RungRead, FoundOnRung, BelowCeiling }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data a_host_property_refusal_missing_from_the_infra_allowlist: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_host_property_refusal_missing_from_the_infra_allowlist" as NonEmptyStr,

  // THE TYPED STANDING MIRRORS WHAT THE THREE SPECIMEN RECEIPTS MEASURED: each refusal was EXECUTED
  // and observed (MemoryEnvelopeAbsent, MemoryReceiptUnreadable/CgroupFileUnreadable,
  // HostBudgetUnreadable on two runner hosts), the class is mitigated by re-placement on a bounded
  // slot and by reading the named owning authority before hunting the diff -- mitigation, not
  // prevention, because every unenumerated host-property cause still lands in the structural bucket.
  // The ceiling is the classifier repair the RECOGNITION RULE receipt names; the blocker is
  // ClimbableButUnbuilt (the arm shape is writable, nothing awaits a declaration).
  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "the floor step's infra-signature reclassifier carries a named arm per KNOWN host-property cause, keyed on WHERE the property lives (the missing host memory interface attributes to the runner slot regardless of which reading step noticed it), attribution-only with the refusal preserved and unknown causes staying structural by default" } },

  receipts: [
    "**a refusal whose cause is a property of the host is attributed to the subject because its signature is not in the floor step's infra allowlist** (the reclassifier is an enumeration of known infra signatures, so any NEW host-side refusal -- a cgroup file the runner lacks, a mount the slot never got, a quota the pool changed -- defaults to the structural bucket and reads as a defect in what was built rather than in where it ran.",

    "ATTRIBUTION ONLY, NEVER ABSOLUTION (manager ruling, framed on the governing ruling memory_envelope_is_part_of_the_verdict): reclassifying an infra signature may change ONLY WHO the failure is attributed to -- the runner slot, whose shape is owned by gunbc.runner.runner_slot_desired -- never WHETHER the run fails. The refusal must keep failing the lane; silent pass and silent retry are both forbidden, because a subject step that refuses an unbounded slot is the ruling working, not malfunctioning. The defect this row carries is the DEFAULT, not the refusal: unmodeled causes fall toward subject attribution, and a reader of floor_class=structural goes hunting in the diff.",

    "SPECIMEN, GitHub Actions run 39980978427 (gunbc, v2-bootstrap lane, branch lane16/red-claim-b-reason at 012f1ed61d26, 2026-10-23). The witness step exited 2 printing MEMORY ENVELOPE REFUSED cause=MemoryEnvelopeAbsent -- GUNBC_MEMORY_ENVELOPE_REQUIRED=slot requires a cgroup memory.max, and no cgroup on the job's path to the root carries a numeric memory.max -- and the step classified the failure floor_class=structural, because the emitted step's infra-signature reclassifier enumerates a fixed allowlist (the page-thrash stall signature, the sccache signatures, the spawn failure) and MemoryEnvelopeAbsent is not in it. The diff under test had already been measured green by claim_batch on the named witness module at that same head (22 PASS / 0 FAIL, srv1), so the structural attribution pointed at a subject that was not the cause. The rerun request was filed; both rerun and original were then cancelled as the head advanced (superseded), so whether a re-placement on a bounded slot clears the signature is NOT yet established -- the row files the mis-attribution, not a flake story, and a re-placement result belongs in this row as a later receipt.",

    "SECOND SPECIMEN, SAME CLASS, SIBLING SIGNATURE: GitHub Actions run 39977116830 (gunbc, v2-bootstrap lane, branch lane16/lowered-call-occurrence at 37adf61c6f09, 2026-10-23). After the emit, build, route and population controls all passed, the step exited 2 printing gunbc test: MEMORY RECEIPT REFUSED cause=MemoryReceiptUnreadable -- CgroupFileUnreadable -- /sys/fs/cgroup/system.slice/system-actions_runner.slice/actions-runner@srv3-03.service/memory.events: No such file or directory -- the receipt reader in the stage0 target_invocation_host refuses when a cgroup file the slot model requires is absent from the host it landed on -- and again the emitted step classified floor_class=structural, because MemoryReceiptUnreadable (and its CgroupFileUnreadable detail) is also absent from the infra allowlist. Two independent host-property causes, two different runner hosts (srv1 slot shape, srv3-03 slot shape), same mis-attribution: the allowlist's enumeration cannot cover host-side causes it never enumerated. Both receipts are dated observations naming their runs; the owning authority for what the slot should have is gunbc.runner.runner_slot_desired, and neither receipt claims the subject failed -- every subject control that ran, passed.",

    "THIRD SPECIMEN, SAME CLASS, THIRD SIGNATURE, AND THE COMMON ROOT MADE VISIBLE: GitHub Actions run 39981233111 (gunbc, heal-generated-artifacts lane, branch lane16/rfm-drift-receipt at 60d3711f5da4, 2026-10-23). The regen round refused with cause=HostBudgetUnreadable -- no modeled host memory source answered (no cgroup memory.high, memory.max or v1 hierarchical_memory_limit binds this process, and GUNBC_MEMORY_BUDGET_BYTES cannot verify one), so the planning allowance is UNKNOWN and dag/gunbc/regen_affected_set.dag refuses rather than admit against the widest signal available -- which is the arm WORKING as its own receipt records: the previous default was the ceiling and OOM-killed the process at rc=137, and the substituted machine-memory arm was SIGKILLed the same way; gunbc.host.host_budget_source owns the budget-source rule, gunbc.runner.runner_slot_desired owns the slot that was not shaped right. Three signatures now -- MemoryEnvelopeAbsent, MemoryReceiptUnreadable/CgroupFileUnreadable, HostBudgetUnreadable -- on two runner hosts, all three reading the ABSENT cgroup memory interface: one host defect, mis-attributed three ways because the allowlist enumerates signatures rather than the property. The repair is one arm shape at the classifier, attribution-only: a refusal whose cause is a MISSING HOST MEMORY INTERFACE attributes to the runner slot, whatever the reading step that noticed it calls itself.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: a structural floor failure whose printed cause names a HOST OR SLOT PROPERTY (cgroup memory files, mounts, quotas, provisioning) rather than a subject artifact is this class until the slot authority itself says otherwise -- check gunbc.runner.runner_slot_desired for the slot the job should have had, and attribute there first. The repair is to the allowlist's completeness (every host-property cause classified by WHERE the property lives, attribution-only, refusal preserved), and -- because a completion predicate over signatures is its own known trap -- the classifier's residual must stay structural-by-default for UNKNOWN causes while each KNOWN host-property cause is enumerated; the fix adds named arms, it does not invert the default.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
